    <string name="app_nombre">NexaPDF</string>
    <string name="ayuda_convertir_c">The Convert tool works both ways: pick a Word, Excel or PowerPoint file and it becomes a PDF; pick a PDF and you choose the format to export to. Tables in the PDF are detected and come out as real tables in Word. What you get is the content recomposed as well as possible, not the original Office file: a PDF stores letters placed on a page, not paragraphs or cells.</string>
    <string name="ayuda_convertir_t">Converting to Word, Excel or PowerPoint</string>
    <string name="ayuda_donde_c">In the Downloads/NexaPDF folder of your phone, where any file manager or app can open them. From the app you can also share them or save a copy wherever you like.</string>
    <string name="ayuda_donde_t">Where are the files I create?</string>
    <string name="ayuda_editar_c">Yes, line by line. Pick the text tool and tap a line: NexaPDF covers the old line and writes yours in its place, as real selectable text. It does not reflow the rest of the paragraph, because a PDF stores fixed positions rather than a flowing document.</string>
    <string name="ayuda_editar_t">Can I change the text of a PDF?</string>
    <string name="ayuda_firmar_c">The handwritten one is a drawing on the page: fine for a delivery note or an internal form. The certificate one uses your .p12 or .pfx file and lets any reader verify that the document has not changed since you signed it: that is the one for anything official.</string>
    <string name="ayuda_firmar_t">Which signature should I use?</string>
    <string name="ayuda_partir_c">Merging works in two steps: first put the documents in order, then the pages of the whole. Add them one at a time or several at once with the + button, and drag by the handle to reorder.

To split, «Split into parts…» shows every page at once. Each part has its own colour: pick the part, tap its first page and then its last, and that stretch is painted in. You can also type the range. Each part keeps the name you give it.</string>
    <string name="ayuda_partir_t">Merging and splitting</string>
    <string name="ayuda_privacidad_c">Nowhere. NexaPDF has no internet permission at all, so it cannot send anything even by mistake. Everything happens inside your device, and the results are saved to Downloads/NexaPDF.</string>
    <string name="ayuda_privacidad_t">Where do my documents go?</string>
    <string name="ayuda_problemas_c">If a document will not open, it may be damaged or protected: try opening it in another reader first. If the app runs out of memory with a very large file, split it into parts and work on them one at a time. For anything else, write to %1$s and say what you were doing.</string>
    <string name="ayuda_problemas_t">Something is not working</string>
    <string name="ayuda_que_es_c">A toolbox for PDFs that runs entirely on your phone. Merge, split, turn photos into documents, draw and write on pages, and sign. No account, no internet, no ads.</string>
    <string name="ayuda_que_es_t">What is NexaPDF?</string>
    <string name="ayuda_titulo">Help</string>
    <string name="ayuda_visor_c">Open a document with Read PDF, or tap one in Recent files. The magnifier searches the whole document: matches are highlighted on the page and the arrows move between them. The list icon shows the document’s sections, if it has any, and the shield lists its digital signatures. Pinch to zoom and drag to move around.</string>
    <string name="ayuda_visor_t">Reading a PDF</string>
